@.str.126 = private unnamed_addr constant [3448 x i8] c" img1 img2 [...imgN] [flags]\0A\0AFlags:\0A  --preview\0A      Run stitching in the preview mode. Works faster than usual mode,\0A      but output image will have lower resolution.\0A  --try_cuda (yes|no)\0A      Try to use CUDA. The default value is 'no'. All default values\0A      are for CPU mode.\0A\0AMotion Estimation Flags:\0A  --work_megapix <float>\0A      Resolution for image registration step. The default is 0.6 Mpx.\0A  --features (surf|orb|sift|akaze)\0A      Type of features used for images matching.\0A      The default is surf if available, orb otherwise.\0A  --matcher (homography|affine)\0A      Matcher used for pairwise image matching.\0A  --estimator (homography|affine)\0A      Type of estimator used for transformation estimation.\0A  --match_conf <float>\0A      Confidence for feature matching step. The default is 0.65 for surf and 0.3 for orb.\0A  --conf_thresh <float>\0A      Threshold for two images are from the same panorama confidence.\0A      The default is 1.0.\0A  --ba (no|reproj|ray|affine)\0A      Bundle adjustment cost function. The default is ray.\0A  --ba_refine_mask (mask)\0A      Set refinement mask for bundle adjustment. It looks like 'x_xxx',\0A      where 'x' means refine respective parameter and '_' means don't\0A      refine one, and has the following format:\0A      <fx><skew><ppx><aspect><ppy>. The default mask is 'xxxxx'. If bundle\0A      adjustment doesn't support estimation of selected parameter then\0A      the respective flag is ignored.\0A  --wave_correct (no|horiz|vert)\0A      Perform wave effect correction. The default is 'horiz'.\0A  --save_graph <file_name>\0A      Save matches graph represented in DOT language to <file_name> file.\0A      Labels description: Nm is number of matches, Ni is number of inliers,\0A      C is confidence.\0A\0ACompositing Flags:\0A  --warp (affine|plane|cylindrical|spherical|fisheye|stereographic|compressedPlaneA2B1|compressedPlaneA1.5B1|compressedPlanePortraitA2B1|compressedPlanePortraitA1.5B1|paniniA2B1|paniniA1.5B1|paniniPortraitA2B1|paniniPortraitA1.5B1|mercator|transverseMercator)\0A      Warp surface type. The default is 'spherical'.\0A  --seam_megapix <float>\0A      Resolution for seam estimation step. The default is 0.1 Mpx.\0A  --seam (no|voronoi|gc_color|gc_colorgrad)\0A      Seam estimation method. The default is 'gc_color'.\0A  --compose_megapix <float>\0A      Resolution for compositing step. Use -1 for original resolution.\0A      The default is -1.\0A  --expos_comp (no|gain|gain_blocks|channels|channels_blocks)\0A      Exposure compensation method. The default is 'gain_blocks'.\0A  --expos_comp_nr_feeds <int>\0A      Number of exposure compensation feed. The default is 1.\0A  --expos_comp_nr_filtering <int>\0A      Number of filtering iterations of the exposure compensation gains.\0A      Only used when using a block exposure compensation method.\0A      The default is 2.\0A  --expos_comp_block_size <int>\0A      BLock size in pixels used by the exposure compensator.\0A      Only used when using a block exposure compensation method.\0A      The default is 32.\0A  --blend (no|feather|multiband)\0A      Blending method. The default is 'multiband'.\0A  --blend_strength <float>\0A      Blending strength from [0,100] range. The default is 5.\0A  --output <result_img>\0A      The default is 'result.jpg'.\0A  --timelapse (as_is|crop) \0A      Output warped images separately as frames of a time lapse movie, with 'fixed_' prepended to input file names.\0A  --rangewidth <int>\0A      uses range_width to limit number of images to match with.\0A\00", align 1
